Z||000000||frontal lobe||07-16-2001||06:38 PM||||Hey, I'm providing a handy link for some interesting reading for you: <A HREF="http://www.cbs.sportsline.com/b/page/pressbox/0,1328,4097781,00.html" TARGET=_blank>www.cbs.sportsline.com/b/page/pressbox/0,1328,4097781,00.html</A>  .  See, this is what I was saying all last year.  I guess I'm just ahead of the curve.  I'm not against having him as a favorite player, just that he is over-rated and doesn't belong with the league's elite at the pro bowl.  I still think the Buccaneers were much better off last year and will be much better off this year with Warrick Dunn running the ball.<P>I see my Packer's Antonio Freeman made it.  He deserves it.  Played more like AntoniA last year.<P>Anyone else have any comments on the list?  For example, black88gt?  Still excited about Grbac?||||reg||1
Z||000001||RiceCooker||07-17-2001||12:45 PM||||Thanks for the article. But it's funn, i read that earlier yesterday morning on my Bucs bulletin board.<P>I have to agree with a lot in that article, and i also agree that Alstott is overrated. Much of it has to do with how he is used. He is a halfback and say warrick dunn was injured last year, Alstott would have came in and rushed for 100 yards a game as well. Now before you disagree, I'm not saying he would spin his way out of tackles or anything else like that, but it has much to do with getting a groove. Any back will have a better avg per carry on 20-25 carries than 12-15. <BR>I'm excited about Dunn getting the bulk of the carries this year for several reasons<BR>-He is an excellent feature back and CAN take the beating from opposing defenders (he usually avoids it)<BR>-It will allow him AND the OL to get more of a rythym. <BR>-Alstott willl be used more in the passing game like he was in his rookie year. He caught 65 balls and 4-6 were for TD's. That's because you really can take a size advantage with him in the flat against a LB as opposed to 3 waiting for him in the trenches.<BR>-Needless to say, I am super excited this season.<P>-Black 88GT and I will be trash talking each other until Saturday Dec 29 when the Bucs host the Ravens<P>I think the pack will have a strong year. second in the Central and a wild card spot. Favre is the opposite of Freeman when it comes to pay day. Freeman had his super season in 98 then got a new contract and hasn't showed up since (don't even bring that catch against the Viks up) Favre on the other hand is still going strong and has been reassured how much his team still believes in him. He's gonna come out swinging this year.<P>Maybe it's almost time to start another football thread. Let's shoot for August 1 ETA. But until then, we need to know what to call it. <BR>I never thought last year that posting "Oh, Those Tricky Buccaneers" would be one of the most famous lines in PFF history  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Well that's all for now, and yes i am into the NFL year round like you wouldn't believe.<P>Beware Johnson & Johnson<P>You shouldda seen me go absoultly berserk on draft day when we traded up for Kenyatta Walker. It was like winning the lotto.||||reg||6
Z||000002||frontal lobe||07-17-2001||06:24 PM||||It's funny you mention Alstott in the passing game, because what used to make the Packers afraid was trying to cover Dunn downfield on pass routes with his speed.  They didn't have a linebacker fast enough to cover him, so they would go with 2 linebackers and 5 defensive backs.  But then if the Bucs ran him, their run defense was weakened.  But don't tell Tony about that.<P>I can't wait to hear what the Vi-Queen fans think this year, because Randy Moss has already made it clear that he wants about all the money the team has, so that's going to make less money available for other players and will weaken the team.  They already lost a lot of players.<P>Regarding the famous "Oh, Those Tricky Buccaneers" thread, at least that was a thread with intelligent conversation about a topic.  Not just some lame thread "dogpile" going on now with the sole goal of reaching a thousand posts.  (Do you guys use the term "dogpile" in Canada?  Serious-I don't know.)||||reg||1
